---
description: How to edit the Codoc tool package
alwaysApply: true
---

Read `AGENTS.md` before editing this repo.

This repository is the Codoc Python package (`codoc` CLI). Keep changes scoped to the requested work. Do not add empty placeholder packages. Do not put roadmap, ticket, milestone, or product-vision text into rules, comments, README, or other repo files. Command names and aliases live only in `COMMANDS` in `src/codoc/cli/`.

## Git branches

Use short descriptive branch names (for example `engine-shim` or `pytest-fixtures`). Never create branches whose names start with `cursor/`. After a feature PR merges, delete the local branch and prune remote-tracking refs.

## Tests

Use pytest. Put shared fixtures in `tests/conftest.py` and reusable helpers under `tests/support/`. Prefer fixtures over copied setup (`git_repo`, `tmp_dir`, `run_cli`, `git_repository`, `yaml_file`). Prefer `@pytest.mark.parametrize` when several inputs share the same assertions. Avoid duplicating `_git_repo` / tempdir / CLI runners inside individual test modules.
